From fe7a739c5a176b7e9f0514479feca42e431a0fb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 22:49:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run the stack on a shared cloud server (EC2 + DuckDNS)

All hostnames now come from SECUREHR_DOMAIN in .env (default localhost), so the
same files run on a laptop and on the shared server.

- nginx config becomes a template filled in at startup (keeps the SLO logging);
  serves the Let's Encrypt HTTP challenge on port 80.
- Domain passed to Keycloak's realm import, Jenkins config-as-code, Gitea,
  the backend's issuer/CORS, and Vite; the frontend derives the Keycloak URL
  from its own address.
- KEYCLOAK_COMMAND=start and FRONTEND_TARGET=prod (built static frontend)
  for the server; laptops keep start-dev and the Vite dev server.
- scripts/get-public-certs.sh: Let's Encrypt certificates (and renewal).
- Gitea and Jenkins images no longer require the local mkcert CA file.
- README step 8: EC2, DuckDNS, setup, hardening and team use.

Also fixes nginx failing on Windows checkouts ("40-logrotate.sh: not found"):
.gitattributes keeps shell scripts and container files at LF line endings, and
the nginx image strips CRLF from the script as a fallback.

